From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: The desktop shows a new wallpaper at once.

The desktop kept the old wallpaper until something else had it drawn
again: neither a new picture (WM_SETTINGCHANGE SPI_SETDESKWALLPAPER) nor a
new colour (WM_SYSCOLORCHANGE) made it draw itself. It is drawn again
then, whoever changed it; user32 fades the new background in (Wine patch
0124).
---
diff --git a/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp b/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp
index ac1d9ec..ac90205 100644
--- a/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp
+++ b/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp
@@ -469,6 +469,13 @@ LRESULT CDesktopBrowser::OnSettingChange(UINT uMsg, WPARAM wParam, LPARAM lParam
         _Resize();
     }
 
+    /* Arctic: a new wallpaper, its fit or the desktop's colour shows at once,
+     * whoever set it; user32 fades it in over the old one */
+    if ((uMsg == WM_SETTINGCHANGE && wParam == SPI_SETDESKWALLPAPER) || uMsg == WM_SYSCOLORCHANGE)
+    {
+        ::RedrawWindow(m_hWnd, NULL, NULL, RDW_INVALIDATE | RDW_ERASE | RDW_ALLCHILDREN);
+    }
+
     return 0;
 }
 
